      "mergeID": "6ac7da8e2654b17f38087f8a",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Though there is one other post I've found with this proposition, its activity is very small.  As a PC user with a lot of friends using Quest, searching for worlds to hang out in quickly becomes exhausting when I have to sort through looking at the small dots in the corners to tell if we can all visit or not.\nA simple enough solution to this would be adding a toggle (similar to the \"show community labs\" toggle) to exclusively show cross-platform worlds (in search results at minimum, but ideally in the quick-menus like the Hot section as well).  My current work-around is to save a search for worlds with the author tag for Quest, but since the search saves only allow three queries total, it would be a lot nicer if this wasn't using up a limited resource.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Cross-Platform Search Toggle",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "616bcf9c9408073e81471328",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "With this long requested feature (see other post) not already being in the main menu 2.0 beta I wish I knew why they haven't implemented this yet.\nLike it's clear with the \"active my platform\" section they have the capabilities to filter platform types.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
